      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Zn(OAc)2·2H2O (0.40 mmol, 0.0876 g), Nd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.30 mmol, 0.1315 g), H2L (0.30 mmol, 0.1333 g) and H2L' (0.35 mmol, 0.0785 g) were dissolved in MeOH (50 mL) at room temperature, then 1.00 mol L−1 triethylamine in EtOH (1 mL) was added. The solution was stirred and heated under reflux for 30 min, cooled, and filtered. Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into the filtrate at room temperature; pale yellow crystals were obtained after one month, filtered off, washed with MeOH (5 mL) and dried in air for one week.",
